{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_29","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc 'python3 /workspace/tools.py read unirank-code:INFNet --start-line 30 --lines 90'","aggregated_output":"/bin/bash: warning: setlocale: LC_ALL: cannot change locale (C.UTF-8)\n/bin/bash: warning: setlocale: LC_ALL: cannot change locale (C.UTF-8)\n{\n  \"id\": \"unirank-code:INFNet\",\n  \"url\": \"https://github.com/salmon1802/UniRank/blob/90bb99a60724e975ec565836266fd86dcad0039d/model_zoo/INFNet.py\",\n  \"version\": \"git:90bb99a60724e975ec565836266fd86dcad0039d\",\n  \"access_scope\": \"Full pinned benchmark source for inspection; not proof of equivalence to the original author method.\",\n  \"text_sha256\": \"e3750a73af1ceb6b2be4bf9355b70a9ad356985a3c465ef27238ef7e0f28fb4c\",\n  \"total_lines\": 313,\n  \"start_line\": 30,\n  \"next_line\": 120,\n  \"truncated\": false,\n  \"text\": \"30:                  gpu=-1,\\n31:                  tower_activations=\\\"ReLU\\\",\\n32:                  tower_hidden_units=[128, 64],\\n33:                  embedding_dim=10,\\n34:                  num_layers=3,\\n35:                  expansion_factor=4,\\n36:                  num_tasks=4,\\n37:                  token_dim=64,\\n38:                  num_c_hub_token=4,\\n39:                  num_t_hub_token=2,\\n40:                  net_dropout=0,\\n41:                  accumulation_steps=1,\\n42:                  **kwargs):\\n43:         super(INFNet, self).__init__(feature_map,\\n44:                                      model_id=model_id,\\n45:                                      gpu=gpu,\\n46:                                      **kwargs)\\n47:         self.num_tasks = num_tasks\\n48:         self.feature_map = feature_map\\n49:         self.embedding_dim = embedding_dim\\n50:         self.token_dim = token_dim\\n51:         self.num_c_hub_token = num_c_hub_token\\n52:         self.num_t_shared_hub = num_t_hub_token\\n53:         self.num_s_hub_token = num_tasks  # Each behavior type in the paper has a hub. Here, the types are divided by tasks.\\n54:         self.accumulation_steps = accumulation_steps\\n55:         self.num_field = feature_map.get_num_fields()\\n56: \\n57:         # Track item and non-item feature dimensions\\n58:         self.item_info_dim = 0\\n59:         self.non_item_dim = 0\\n60:         for feat, spec in self.feature_map.features.items():\\n61:             if feat in self.feature_map.labels:\\n62:                 continue\\n63:             if spec.get(\\\"type\\\") == \\\"meta\\\":\\n64:                 continue\\n65:             emb_dim = spec.get(\\\"embedding_dim\\\", embedding_dim)\\n66:             if spec.get(\\\"source\\\") in [\\\"item\\\", \\\"action\\\"]:\\n67:                 self.item_info_dim += emb_dim\\n68:             else:\\n69:                 self.non_item_dim += emb_dim\\n70: \\n71:         self.embedding_layer = FeatureEmbedding(feature_map, embedding_dim)\\n72: \\n73:         # 1. Categorical Tokenization\\n74:         self.unified_tokenizer_layer = INFNetCategoricalTokenizer(\\n75:             embedding_dim=embedding_dim,\\n76:             token_dim=token_dim,\\n77:             num_c_hub_token=num_c_hub_token,\\n78:             num_field=self.num_field,\\n79:             expansion_factor=expansion_factor\\n80:         )\\n81: \\n82:         # 2. Task Tokenization (Specific & Shared)\\n83:         self.task_orgs = nn.init.xavier_uniform_(nn.Parameter(torch.empty(1, self.num_tasks, token_dim)))\\n84:         self.task_shared_hubs = nn.init.xavier_uniform_(nn.Parameter(torch.empty(1, self.num_t_shared_hub, token_dim)))\\n85: \\n86:         # 3. Sequence Tokenization\\n87:         self.seq_org_proj = nn.Linear(self.item_info_dim, token_dim)\\n88:         self.seq_hub_projs = nn.ModuleList([\\n89:             nn.Linear(self.item_info_dim, token_dim) for _ in range(self.num_tasks)\\n90:         ])\\n91:         self.masked_avg_pooling = MaskedAveragePooling()\\n92: \\n93:         # INFNet Stacked Blocks (pass in num_layers to stack layer by layer)\\n94:         self.unified_interaction_layers = INFNetBlocks(\\n95:             num_layers=num_layers,\\n96:             token_dim=token_dim,\\n97:             num_c_hubs=self.num_c_hub_token,\\n98:             num_s_hubs=self.num_s_hub_token,\\n99:             num_t_hubs=self.num_tasks + self.num_t_shared_hub,\\n100:             expansion_factor=expansion_factor)\\n101: \\n102:         # Task Towers\\n103:         self.tower = nn.ModuleList([MLP_Block(input_dim=token_dim,\\n104:                                               output_dim=1,\\n105:                                               hidden_units=tower_hidden_units,\\n106:                                               hidden_activations=tower_activations,\\n107:                                               output_activation=None,\\n108:                                               dropout_rates=net_dropout)\\n109:                                     for _ in range(num_tasks)])\\n110: \\n111:         if isinstance(task, list):\\n112:             assert len(task) == num_tasks, \\\"the number of tasks must equal the length of \\\\\\\"task\\\\\\\"\\\"\\n113:             self.output_activation = nn.ModuleList([self.get_output_activation(str(t)) for t in task])\\n114:         else:\\n115:             self.output_activation = nn.ModuleList(\\n116:                 [self.get_output_activation(task) for _ in range(num_tasks)]\\n117:             )\\n118: \\n119:         self.compile(kwargs.get(\\\"dense_optimizer\\\"), kwargs[\\\"loss\\\"], kwargs.get(\\\"dense_learning_rate\\\"))\"\n}\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_30","type":"agent_message","text":"The latest content summaries offered little advantage over rotated membership controls. That leaves a useful question: does averaging erase interactions that a learned encoder could preserve?\n\nI’ll implement a four-cell study comparing nonlinearity before versus after averaging, crossed with blocked versus shared auxiliary item gradients. The cells will share parameters and the main matrix operations, making compression timing the central contrast. The design draws on target-conditioned DIN pooling and behavior-specific INFNet summaries; it makes no novelty claim. [INFNet paper](https://arxiv.org/pdf/2508.11565v1)\n"}}
