{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_42","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"python3 - <<'PY'\nimport ast, hashlib, json\nfrom pathlib import Path\np=Path('/workspace')\nr=json.load(open(p/'runtime_snapshot.json'))\nc=r['context']; protocol=r['required_study_protocol_ref']\nvariants=[]\nsettings=[('encode_pool_blocked','candidate.py','candidate','before_pool',True),('pool_encode_blocked','pool_then_encode_blocked.py','control','after_pool',True),('encode_pool_shared','encode_then_pool_shared.py','control','before_pool',False),('pool_encode_shared','pool_then_encode_shared.py','control','after_pool',False)]\nhashes={}\nfor name,file,role,timing,blocked in settings:\n source=(p/file).read_text(); tree=ast.parse(source)\n cfg=ast.literal_eval(next(n.value for n in tree.body if isinstance(n,ast.Assign) and any(isinstance(t,ast.Name) and t.id=='CONFIG' for t in n.targets)))\n hashes[file]=hashlib.sha256(source.encode()).hexdigest()\n variants.append({'name':name,'file':file,'role':role,'config':cfg,'note':f'Compression timing={timing}; auxiliary item/action source gradients blocked={blocked}. Same inherited UF/count path, same learned affine event/context/target encoder, same twelve aligned memberships, same three auxiliary readouts and initialization. Only ReLU placement and the declared source gate differ across cells. Source embeddings are detached before the learned encoder in blocked cells; encoder parameters remain trainable. New final readouts start at zero. Host must pass finite forward/backward, masking, gradient ownership, inherited initialization and buffer checks before training. No local numerical execution. SHA256={hashes[file]}.'})\nbase_fixed=['protocol '+protocol,'released 100-position history and masks; all authorized fields only','four unweighted BCE losses; frozen scratch single-pass recipe and paired seed 20262027','UF local activation, Dice state policy, towers and exact-count branch','twelve aligned category/brand/joint memberships crossed with exposure/cart/fav/buy','32-dimensional affine encoder and 32-unit auxiliary readouts; all parameter shapes and initialization','100-event value and product projections; one context/target projection; twelve code reductions','zero-final residual readouts and restored CPU RNG stream']\nproposal={\n 'parent_trial':'g2-r0007-aligned_blocked',\n 'study':{\n  'id':'g2-compression-nonlinearity-timing-factorial',\n  'protocol_ref':protocol,\n  'evidence_refs':['baseline-din','g2-r0000-match20','g2-r0000-rotated20','g2-r0000-uniform10','g2-r0002-uniform_feedback','g2-r0002-uniform_uniform','g2-r0004-context_only','g2-r0004-both','g2-r0005-private_residual','g2-r0005-shared_residual','g2-r0005-blocked_no_residual','g2-r0006-exact_blocked','g2-r0006-support_blocked','g2-r0006-exact_shared','g2-r0007-aligned_blocked','g2-r0007-rotated_blocked','g2-r0007-aligned_shared','g2-r0007-rotated_shared'],\n  'question':'After counts and raw relational means recover auxiliary quality only partially, does applying a learned context/target-conditioned nonlinearity before averaging retain useful event-level interactions at fixed representation capacity, and does its benefit depend on auxiliary access to shared item/action embeddings?',\n  'hypothesis':'Raw means cannot distinguish histories with equal first moments but different event-level interactions. A 32-dimensional learned code z_i = Wv*v_i + Wp*(target*key_i) + Wq*[context,target] + b, rectified per event before masked averaging, may recover auxiliary ranking information absent from ReLU(mean(z_i)). Blocking auxiliary gradients at the source embeddings may preserve click quality while the new dense encoder learns to use those embeddings. This is an unverified explanation of the round7 limitation, not an established mechanism.',\n  'nearest_work':[\n   {'source_ref':'paper:din','verification':'read','difference':'Archived arXiv:1706.06978v4 primary text, lines75-85 and270-277, inspected. Retain the adapted local-activation path. The new branch pools vector-valued rectified target/context-conditioned event codes; it is not a new attention claim or exact DIN reproduction.'},\n   {'source_ref':'paper:infnet','verification':'read','difference':'Authorized original arXiv:2508.11565v1 sections3.1-3.2 inspected. It projects events and pools by behavior, then exchanges information using proxies. Here twelve exact-relation means feed residual auxiliary readouts; the experiment isolates rectification timing and source gradients, without iterative proxy attention or broadcasts.'},\n   {'source_ref':'unirank-code:INFNet','verification':'implementation_checked','difference':'Pinned benchmark source at90bb99a60724e975ec565836266fd86dcad0039d, lines82-91 and123-170 inspected. Its task-specific linear projections precede masked means. The current affine/ReLU timing contrast tests a different adapted encoder; benchmark masked means and original-paper sum pooling are not conflated.'},\n   {'source_ref':'g2-r0007-aligned_blocked','verification':'implementation_checked','difference':'Source hash612e71551cbf3f9b799424806c4dd46178cc675d93ce557c3de15259d549160d verified. Replace its raw-mean/product residual with a narrower learned code residual. Retain exact counts and membership. Absolute comparisons to round7 also change readout parameterization, so the four new matched cells carry the timing attribution.'}\n  ],\n  'inherited_components':['FeatureEmbeddingDict and tied target/history item tables; historical action values only','incumbent uniform-click/feedback-auxiliary UF compression and count-weighted unnormalized DIN activation','functional detached auxiliary scorer and cloned Dice buffers; persistent scorer buffers updated only by primary call','open context source gradients, crossed blocked/shared item/action gradients','round6 exact-count sidecar and its zero-final initialization','round7 twelve aligned exposure/task x category/brand/joint memberships; zero-final auxiliary residual convention'],\n  'proposed_difference':'Replace the round7 moment residual with factorized affine per-event codes conditioned on supplied context, target, target-field products and historical values. Pool ReLU(z) in the candidate; pool z then apply ReLU in its replacement control. Compute the identical projections on100 events in both cells so the principal matrix shapes and parameter count match. Twelve32-dimensional summaries feed task-specific residual heads using three exposure slots plus three task slots, exact counts and the target. Cross timing with the source gradient gate in a2x2 suite. No new click residual, private vocabulary, loss hook, data pass or label access. The primary click effect can occur indirectly through shared context updates, not through a direct code readout.',\n  'predictions':[\n   'Within each source-gate setting, encode_pool should improve auxiliary mean AUC over pool_encode if nonlinear within-group information is useful. Report cart/fav/buy AUC and Logloss individually; mean auxiliary AUC is secondary, never the selection score.',\n   'Blocked cells should reduce the click penalty relative to their shared counterparts. A useful joint outcome would improve auxiliary quality over g2-r0006-exact_blocked and g2-r0007-aligned_blocked without losing click quality relative to incumbent g2-r0004-context_only. No improvement is assumed.',\n   'The timing effect should be small on empty/singleton groups and may be larger for long histories. Existing empty/1-16/17-64/>64 history slices are exploratory interaction evidence because history length is only a proxy for relation-group occupancy.',\n   'All four cells must have identical parameter counts and paired initialization; their new code branch has no batch state. The two gate values must give identical forward predictions for identical state and timing before optimization.',\n   'The timing contrast has equal major projection/reduction shapes but different ReLU tensor lengths (100 versus12). Measure allocated time, wall time, memory and inference; do not infer equal measured cost from matched operators or claim a quality-cost frontier from parameters alone.'\n  ],\n  'falsifiers':[\n   'If encode_pool does not outperform pool_encode in auxiliary AUC/Logloss at either gate setting, this implementation does not support nonlinear preaggregation information retention. If both beat round7 equally, capacity/readout changes rather than timing remain the explanation.',\n   'If the auxiliary timing benefit appears only when item/action gradients are shared and accompanies click deterioration, the proposed protected-source recovery mechanism is not supported.',\n   'If click improves without auxiliary improvement, do not attribute it to recovered auxiliary history information; changed context optimization remains plausible. A single seed establishes only a provisional observation.',\n   'Any masked-history or target-action dependence, current-label access, incorrect task ordering, unplanned shared embedding alias, stale source gate, nonfinite output/gradient or inherited-initialization mismatch invalidates the affected comparison before scientific interpretation.',\n   'If even the better cell misses the incumbent click AUC on full validation, retain the incumbent for selection. A null or negative outcome remains reportable and does not refute DIN, INFNet or all encode-before-pool mechanisms.'\n  ],\n  'alternative_explanations':[\n   'Click-trained embeddings may lack auxiliary information that a dense encoder cannot recover; round5 private ID capacity recovered more auxiliary quality but added24.26M parameters and substantial time.',\n   'ReLU placement changes optimization and feature scale as well as representational distinguishability. A positive contrast alone is not a proof of a sufficient statistic or a general information-theoretic mechanism.',\n   'Shared context updates couple auxiliary and click objectives even with item gradients blocked. Parameter aliases must be audited before interpreting gates as ownership of disjoint tables.',\n   'Relation groups may be sparse or empty, and missing category/brand IDs are excluded from joins. The suite does not isolate relation membership itself, query conditioning, temporal order or the full32-dimensional width.',\n   'New heads are narrower than round7 and have different target/context routes. Cross-round absolute gains cannot isolate timing; only within-suite replacements do.',\n   'All historical comparisons are single-seed, and repeated same-seed endpoints are consistency checks. Validation adaptation, user clustering and rare auxiliary positives limit confidence.',\n   'BF16 summation, runtime scheduling and pointwise activation counts may yield small cost/numerical differences despite matching principal matrix shapes. No post-pooling optimization that changes execution cost is included in this suite.'\n  ],\n  'contrasts':[\n   {'parent_ref':'g2-r0007-aligned_blocked','intervention':'encode_pool_blocked: mean(ReLU(z)) with auxiliary item/action sources detached before encoding','control':'pool_encode_blocked: ReLU(mean(z)) using the identical encoder, groups and readouts','held_fixed':base_fixed+['block_aux_item_grad=True; context open; auxiliary scorer parameters blocked'], 'remaining_confounds':['ReLU placement necessarily changes gradients and feature scale; equal parameter count is not proof of equal optimization difficulty','pointwise operation counts differ; measured time is required'],'decision_if_supported':'Retain as provisional evidence that preaggregation nonlinearity helps this protected-source auxiliary branch; reserve paired repetition and a later information/optimization control before mechanism claims.','decision_if_not_supported':'Reject this implementation as an improvement over its replacement; retain the null and consider whether the observed limitation is source representation rather than compression timing.'},\n   {'parent_ref':'g2-r0007-aligned_shared','intervention':'encode_pool_shared: mean(ReLU(z)) with auxiliary item/action source gradients open','control':'pool_encode_shared: ReLU(mean(z)) with the same open source gradients','held_fixed':base_fixed+['block_aux_item_grad=False; context open; auxiliary scorer parameters blocked'],'remaining_confounds':['source embeddings adapt under auxiliary gradients; changes can affect primary click predictions','same nonlinearity/optimization distinction as the blocked contrast'],'decision_if_supported':'Compare its auxiliary effect and click cost with the blocked contrast; a shared-only gain motivates a representation-learning follow-up rather than claiming blocked-source recovery.','decision_if_not_supported':'Do not generalize a null beyond this width/recipe; compare the blocked contrast and preserve the failed trajectory.'},\n   {'parent_ref':'g2-r0007-aligned_blocked','intervention':'Gate contrasts encode_pool_blocked versus encode_pool_shared and pool_encode_blocked versus pool_encode_shared; estimate the difference of their timing effects','control':'The other timing cell is the factorial interaction control; g2-r0006-exact_blocked/exact_shared and all round7 cells remain historical references','held_fixed':base_fixed,'remaining_confounds':['the gate affects every auxiliary item/action path, not only the new encoder; the interaction is descriptive for the complete architecture','the underlying AUC is nonlinear and single-seed effects have no independent uncertainty estimate'],'decision_if_supported':'Separate source protection from timing and report the interaction rather than a single favorable cell. Compare incumbent, DIN, exact-count and round7 costs and all four tasks.','decision_if_not_supported':'Report additive/null/reversed interaction faithfully; do not count multiple seeds or historical endpoints as independent mechanism contrasts.'}\n  ],\n  'cost_plan':{\n   'estimate_ref':'g2-r0006-exact_blocked wall301.47s; g2-r0007-aligned_blocked316.74s and aligned_shared336.89s; g2-r0005-private_residual435.13s. Frozen protocol estimated_unit_seconds481.35 and per-trial cap1203.3689693547785s. The new100-event narrow projections add work: provisional350-650s/cell, unmeasured.',\n   'all_variants_counted':True,\n   'attribution_reserve':'Four submitted cells consume at most4813.48s at the existing per-trial cap, plus preparation and host correctness costs. Reserve12000s for discriminating follow-ups and paired repetitions, including failed attempts; do not spend this reserve on routine tuning. Snapshot remaining157152.68s is inherited, not a refreshed ledger.',\n   'assessment_reserve':'Reserve10000s for final paired repetitions, baseline/incumbent/closest-control comparisons, suite freezing and host assessment when that phase is authorized. Current phase requests no holdout scoring; final suite and repetitions must be frozen before any such request.',\n   'stop_rule':'No training or installations in this coding workspace. The host must charge all preparation, checks, attempts and evaluations to the existing172800s research wall budget/deadline and enforce1203.3689693547785s per trial. Never raise either. Stop or retain the incumbent if correctness fails, hard limits bind, or no informative admissible contrast plus reserved attribution/assessment fits.'\n  }\n },\n 'variants':variants,\n 'artifact_hashes':hashes,\n 'evidence_review':[],\n 'host_prerequisites':[\n  'Use the already frozen pinned dataset identity9f110bfc2f037f36e2f48787b812df640fe5df2de1cda8db7ac04590c1c9be44 and protocol; no raw-data verification or re-acquisition is available in this jail. Source hashes of the baseline, incumbent source and four supplied round7 ancestors matched their declared receipts.',\n  'Instantiate each module with the actual FeatureMap. Verify four finite [B,1] probabilities and default finite sum-BCE backward in FP32 and frozen BF16; host optimizer must register all new projections/heads as dense parameters. No custom loss is supplied.',\n  'Audit actual embedding aliases and source dimensions. Check isolated auxiliary losses give zero gradient to shared item/action tables in blocked cells and to local_activation in every cell; context remains open. Check new encoder gradient after setting a nonzero final readout or after a controlled optimizer step: zero-final heads intentionally yield zero encoder gradient on the first backward.',\n  'Compare same-seed state_dicts and post-constructor CPU RNG state for all four cells. Inherited embedding/scorer/tower/count tensors must equal the round6 ancestor; zero code readouts must reproduce its initialized probabilities. Confirm only the primary scorer call updates persistent Dice buffers.',\n  'Mask tests: empty, singleton, short and full history; overlapping task masks; absent/missing category and brand; target-action perturbation; padding-value perturbation and arbitrary holes with fixed masks. Only test the new summary as permutation-invariant within each fixed membership; the inherited UF operator retains its temporal blocks.',\n  'Operator check on synthetic tensors: with fixed query, linear projection and empty/nonempty memberships, mean(z) equals projecting the raw group mean for nonempty groups (including its query/bias); empty group code is exactly zero. For one hidden coordinate, events+a and-a versus0 and0 have equal raw mean but unequal mean(ReLU(z)); after-pool ReLU cannot distinguish them. Disabling ReLU in a test copy must make timing cells agree within dtype tolerance. These are implementation checks, not data evidence.',\n  'All correctness gates remain unexecuted locally because torch is absent. Do not treat static success as host execution success; preserve and charge any host failure receipt. No duplicate retry on unknown execution state.'\n ],\n 'evaluation_plan':{\n  'selection':'Full-population validation is_click ROC-AUC only. Keep g2-r0004-context_only as the incumbent until supported validation improvement. Report differences from both that incumbent and the closest exact-count/round7 controls.',\n  'factorial_estimands':['click and auxiliary per-task/mean AUC and Logloss encode_pool minus pool_encode at each gate','blocked minus shared within each timing','difference of timing effects between blocked and shared; descriptive until paired repetition'],\n  'costs':['parameters and dense/embedding split','allocated GPU seconds and wall seconds, examples/data passes','peak GPU memory','inference examples/s and batch p50/p95 latency under host protocol'],\n  'slices':'Use host-provided predeclared empty/1-16/17-64/>64 history bins with sample/positive/negative counts. Other slices only if the authorized host provides them; do not invent raw timestamps, IDs, training-frequency data or relation-occupancy diagnostics. Mark post-hoc slice interpretations exploratory.',\n  'uncertainty':'Current suite uses the frozen paired seed20262027. Target three paired seeds for a consequential candidate and matched control in a later authorized phase if resources permit; user-cluster bootstrap only if authorized predictions and cluster identities are actually available to the evaluator. Do not invent intervals, claim significance from these runs or treat same-seed endpoint replays as independent repetitions.',\n  'withheld':'Closed; no assessment requested or holdout-dependent selection. No new measured performance is included in this proposal.'\n },\n 'knowledge_assessments':[],\n 'preparation_record':{\n  'phase':'propose',\n  'previous_runtime_error':c['previous_runtime_error'],\n  'local_checks_completed':['Verified declared baseline/incumbent/round7 source SHA256s','All four modules parse and compile as Python source without imports','Literal CONFIG values match constructor defaults','Normalized ASTs differ only by code_timing and block_aux_item_grad defaults/config values','Inherited _count_statistics, _compress_both, _interactions, _auxiliary_activation and _pool ASTs equal the round7 ancestor','Model